From: LuneOS <webos-ports@googlegroups.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ussd: accept pre-decoded UTF-8 from drivers (dcs 0xff)

Sailfish's oFono treats dcs 0xff in ofono_ussd_notify() as "the driver
already produced a NUL-terminated UTF-8 string", using the buffer as-is
instead of running it through ussd_decode(), and frees it afterwards.

ofono-binder-plugin depends on that contract - binder_ussd.c duplicates
the message with gutil_memdup() specifically because the core frees it:

    /* Message is freed by core if dcs is 0xff, we have to duplicate it. */
    ofono_ussd_notify(self->ussd, type, 0xff, gutil_memdup(msg, len+1), len);

Upstream does not know the convention, so 0xff reaches ussd_decode(),
cbs_dcs_decode() rejects it as an invalid coding scheme, NULL comes back
and the D-Bus reply carries an empty string. Observed on sargo/mindphone:
"ussd length 35" in the plugin, then an empty response for every USSD
query. The core already g_free()s utf8_str, and gutil_memdup() allocates
with g_malloc(), so ownership transfer is correct.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [oFono fork specific]

--- a/src/ussd.c
+++ b/src/ussd.c
@@ -432,8 +432,22 @@
 		goto out;
 	}
 
-	if (data && data_len > 0)
-		utf8_str = ussd_decode(dcs, data_len, data);
+	if (data && data_len > 0) {
+		if (dcs == 0xff)
+			/*
+			 * Sailfish convention, which the binder plugin
+			 * relies on: dcs 0xff means the driver already
+			 * handed us a NUL-terminated UTF-8 string rather
+			 * than an encoded PDU. It duplicates the buffer
+			 * precisely because the core frees it below, so
+			 * take ownership and skip the decode - passing
+			 * 0xff to ussd_decode() makes cbs_dcs_decode()
+			 * fail and the response comes out empty.
+			 */
+			utf8_str = (char *) data;
+		else
+			utf8_str = ussd_decode(dcs, data_len, data);
+	}
 
 	str = utf8_str;
 
